{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Independently filtered next documentation batch\n\nSurvey baseline. The dedicated worktree is clean at origin/main commit ce496143fe1f72a07efeb0173da37013262ec446. The approved epic unhygenic-gabby-indianhare is closed without force. Two independent filters challenged every candidate against the files, ticket history, ADRs, audience policy, and rejected enforcement proposals.\n\n### F14 Server manifest record parity\n\nThe current checker compares only environment names. It cannot detect changed descriptions, duplicate names, or incorrect isRequired fields. Compare a normalized projection of name, description, and isRequired between MCP_ENV_VARS and server.json. Treat isRequired as false for every optional environment value. Reject duplicate names and ignore record order and JSON formatting. read-grape-coin established MCP_ENV_VARS as the source and required accurate descriptions. It did not reject full field comparison. Verification uses focused checker fixtures and the checker command. This is contract drift detection, not prose enforcement.\n\n### F15 Adoption template accuracy\n\ntemplates/rebar-usage.md and its synchronized region in templates/AGENTS.md teach an unconditional bare assignee and list six relations. Teach rebar claim without an explicit assignee when ticket.default_assignee is configured. Permit an explicit project identity when no default exists. Require email or accountId for Jira reconciled stores. Add caused_by and dependency order review guidance. bilingual-raptorial-furseal deliberately left these templates unchanged because adopter repositories may lack a default assignee. The conditional fallback resolves that recorded concern. stun-wraith-conch, weariless-scrapable-mouse, isogonal-wedded-catfish, and dolorous-coverable-mice establish the behavior and synchronized source. Preserve the existing byte synchronization test and add only focused behavior assertions.\n\n### F16 Static demonstration correction\n\ndocs/assets/rebar-demo.svg uses a deprecated four digit reference, an unconditional bare assignee, stale displayed output, and narration that no longer matches the workflow. Replace the interaction with supported aliases or two quad identifiers and command output verified against current CLI contracts. Remove the unconditional assignee. Preserve the static, text editable SVG decision on weak-amenable-worm. Do not add a generator. Preserve the existing role, aria-label, and README alternative text mechanisms, updating their wording only when the displayed content changes. Verification renders the SVG and inspects it at normal and narrow display sizes. No full test suite is needed for this documentation asset.\n\n### F17 Example agent workflow correction\n\nexamples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md teaches explicit bare assignees and offers direct transition as an alternative to atomic claim. examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md calls an unsigned claimability fast fail a successful review cycle. Use atomic claim with the F15 identity fallback. State that a blocked ticket defers review until it becomes claimable and that the unsigned INDETERMINATE result is not a successful verdict. Preserve dependency order and the prohibition on agent force. comely-craven-apatosaur and stealthful-calmy-erin establish the enforced behavior. Append a correction to arid-gutless-myna because that historical record introduced the inaccurate success wording. Verification uses focused skill contract checks.\n\n### F18 User guide audience correction\n\ndocs/user-guide.md is the human workflow guide established by handmade-radical-johndory. Its relation inventory omits caused_by. It also explains top level router extraction, blame selection internals, a dated credential incident, and session pointer resolution. Add caused_by. Keep user visible mutation output, attribution, secret screening, session log behavior, and recovery actions. Replace implementation and incident narration with concise behavior and references to internal documentation or coyish-fluent-gibbon where history remains useful. Preserve supported command examples and safety guidance. Run documentation index checks and focused user guide contracts. Skip the full suite because this unit changes Markdown only. The lower README cleanup is not included.\n\n### F20 Historical citation correction\n\naimless-seclusive-tigershark cites ADR 0018 as authority for plan review before claim. ADR 0018 governs the T5c trust boundary scope gate. Append a correction that cites messy-moose-jig and docs/plan-review-gate.md for claim enforcement. Preserve the original description and GitHub metadata. Verification is ticket readback only.\n\n### F29 Contributor tutorial correction\n\ndocs/your-first-change.md still downloads the Gerrit hook directly, permits a tiny patch to skip Gerrit, and recommends recheck when a failure only looks flaky. Replace direct hook installation with make hooks. State that a maintainer may sponsor a change while every main change still passes Gerrit. Reserve recheck for demonstrated environmental faults and direct nondeterministic test failures to root cause work. fat-leaflike-canary introduced the tutorial. sultanlike-doughty-civet and sure-starred-springtail superseded its hook and retry instructions. Extend the focused guidance contract or add a narrow tutorial contract, then run documentation link checks. Do not run the full suite.\n\n### F30A RP-04 architecture correction\n\ndocs/architecture.md says RP-04 is unimplemented. docs/reuse-surface.md says its diagnostic shadow will be removed in S7. RP-04 is closed, but REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW remains enabled by default and diagnostic only for the legacy shadow surfaces. Describe the implemented OperationSnapshot composer, runtime bindings, provider authentication carriers, ownership gate, and the remaining diagnostic boundary without claiming the snapshot controls every operation. vibrant-legal-hind, ADR 0098, and opal-daffy-mutt establish this qualified state. Do not change ADR 0098 or runtime behavior. Verify links and focused operation snapshot documentation contracts.\n\n### F30B RP-05 architecture correction\n\ndocs/architecture.md says RP-05 remains pending. The module docstring in src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py still calls the registry shadow scaffolding. The closed grapy-cynical-copepod epic and pettish-snippy-rasbora record the completed cutover. Describe ROUTES, lazy handler and parser references, runtime registry dispatch, generated help inputs, and CAPABILITIES as the implemented boundary. Correct the stale module docstring. Do not change ADR 0100 or registry behavior. Run focused registry, help coverage, generation, and import isolation checks.\n\n### F31 Event contract correction\n\ndocs/event-schema.md presents retired shell files as current writers and omits several recognized event categories from its main contract. Replace writer names with maintained producer seams. Add KEY_ADD and KEY_REVOKE to replayed types. Separate reducer ignored sidecars from replay mutations. Classify PRECONDITIONS and SYNC as recognized non replay records. Name the direct BRIDGE_ALERT producer and remove the deleted writer footnote. barky-suit-dial began the accepted documentation truth sweep but left the historical shell names in the current table. Preserve sidecar and compatibility semantics. Do not add a generated catalog while F05 remains deferred. Run focused event schema contracts and documentation checks.\n\n### F38 Maintenance runbook correction\n\ndocs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md calls the enforced 800 line module limit a soft cap. It also embeds a dated tool inventory, machine state, measurements, findings, and capture debris as maintained procedure. Keep a project adapter that points to examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/SKILL.md for the audit phases, retains project gate commands, and overrides the generic artifact option with rebar session logs and tickets for this repository. State that the module limit is an absolute CI gate sourced from .github/module-size-limit.txt. Remove dated observations from the procedure and preserve history through its tickets. unafraid-homey-umbrette records the complexity ratchet and scabby-slur-junk records a prior audit finding. Verification executes the documented read only commands and checks documentation links. Skip the full suite.\n\n### Held items\n\nF23 and the lower README rewrite remain held. The plan guide and lower README contain accepted guidance added by several later tickets, and neither candidate has a complete destination map for displaced content. F05 remains deferred. F02, F03, and F04 remain rejected. No retained item adds mechanical prose or character enforcement."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787506292351880001,"uuid":"ebd997a6-ee1f-48a6-8f48-2bbf448973a2"}